ad another benefit too it  contained vitamin C and eaten in  relatively High quantities it just about  staved off the ravages of scurvy when  food was plentiful the two men dried to  fish and meat in the sun on the side of  the boat but when times were desperate  they swallowed whatever they could get  their hands on Gollum style and it was  his habit of necessity that brought  about the Journey's great tragedy  after consuming a meal of raw seabird  Cordoba fell quite suddenly ill and it  soon became clear why inside the bird's  stomach was the half-eating remains of a  poisonous sea snake Cordoba survived the  incident but he was never quite the same  he started refusing food entirely and in  his already weakened State his condition  quickly deteriorated four months into  the journey he passed away  alvaranga was understandably devastated  the two men had grown quite close during  their ordeal and with cordoba's death  alvarenga had not only lost a friend  he'd lost his only link to humanity  the previous four months have been one  long battle against the elements against  starvation and dehydration and against  the constant fear that the fish would  wise up or the rain would stay away just  a few days too long but with the passing  of Ezekiel Cordoba alvarenga had found  himself facing off against another far  deadlier enemy total isolation the  prospect of being alone in that  desperate situation was so terrible that  at first alvarenga simply couldn't face  it he kept cordoba's body with him in  the boat chatting away with his young  friend as if he was still alive  for six full days he chatted to the  corpse whilst nature took its course  until he finally realized he was losing  his mind  the two men had come to an agreement  that should one of them die the other  wouldn't eat the body so alvarenga said  a few quiet words of farewell to his  former friend then rolled him solemnly  overboard he wouldn't set eyes on  another human being for close to a year  of course the oceans aren't entirely  empty and alvarenga frequently saw ships  passing by on the horizon container  ships mostly  colossal floating mini cities that  Traverse some of the most remote parts  of our planet's 139 million square miles  of ocean but despite being some of the  biggest vessels in existence container  ships invariably have very small Crews  usually no more than 20 to 30 people so  eyes on the ocean are limited  alvarenga's tiny skiff was little more  than a speck amongst the endless waves  and he was never spotted it's impossible  to imagine what he must have gone  through as those long months ambled by  we live in an age where people won't  even sit on the toilet for five minutes  without their mobile phones for fear of  being subjected to the tyranny of  boredom Jose Salvador alvarenga spent 10  months alone in a tiny boat with  absolutely nothing  and yet despite the hardships the  dangers and against all the odds he  clung to life day after day month after  month and then one morning his Slumber  was stirred by something strange a flock  of birds circling overhead  seabirds weren't a particularly uncommon  sight for alvarenga he'd murdered his  fair share over the previous 14 months  after all but these weren't like any  seabirds he'd come to know in the past  year or so and there is good reason for  that they weren't seabirds alvarenga  scrambled to his feet and there in the  distance he saw it land  the skiff drifted over the coral barrier  that surrounded what he would later  learn was Eben at all and he dived  headfirst into the water minutes later  the waves tossed his battered body onto  the beach as bad as things had been for  Jose Salvador alvarenga and make no  mistake they had been impossibly  unfathomably bad that moment falling  onto the beach and feeling the sand  between his fingers must have been one  of the most Exquisite experienced by any  human being ever  for the first time in more than a year  his feet were firmly on dry land  ebonotal is a rough Circle comprising 22  separate islands and the one alvarenga  happened to have landed on tile islet  was smaller than a football pitch and  entirely uninhabited but only a few  meters separated from NN itok to the  north and it was there that Russell and  Emmy heard his cries bringing our story  full circle  it feels a bit ridiculous to call Jose  alvarenga lucky but it's worth pointing  out that Eben atoll is the only land for  at least 100 miles in any direction it's  one of the most remote places on the  planet and if his path had been just a  few miles to the North or South he'd  have drifted clean past it the next stop  would likely have been the Philippines  more than 3 000 miles away it's  difficult to sum up a story like  alvarenus it's one of those things the  human brain just isn't capable of  comprehending like the size of the  universe or the price of beer in London  put simply Jose Salvador alvarenga's 438  days at Sea represent one of the most  remarkable Journeys and feat of survival  ever endured by a human being  thanks for watching
 

